00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:29.060
Tarkin in Rogue One, animating the
movement of the lips and the jaw in an

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:32.840
authentic way is really difficult for
even the best artists to pull off. So you

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:36.290
know, just show Snoke in super-tight,
extreme close-ups from the nose up and

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.230
you'll be as golden as Snoke's robes.
Which... yeah.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:42.260
They're gold. What's the deal with that?
Now Snoke appears to be torturing Rey

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:49.200
here, suspending her body and causing her
to shake violently. And notice what he says: "Fulfill your destiny!"

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:53.200
This is exactly what Emperor Palpatine
said to Luke before torturing him with

00:14:53.210 --> 00:14:58.040
sith lightning in Return of the Jedi.
"Fulfill your destiny!" I think the takeaway

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:02.840
here is that Rey, after being rejected by
Luke, will seek to continue her training

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:07.190
and learn the truth about her origin, even if
it means turning to the dark side. When

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:11.260
really, Snoke would only want to use her
for her raw, untamed power. Let's move on

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:12.580
to this final section.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:20.920
"I need someone... to show me my place in all this."

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:34.560
Okay, as I mentioned before, this trailer
has clearly been edited to misdirect us.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:37.660
I think this final exchange is another
example of it. While I do think it's

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:41.320
possible that Rey reaches out to the
dark side in search of answers and

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:43.780
training, I don't think that's what's
happening here.

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:46.810
I just don't think these shots of Rey are
from the same scene. There's three pieces

00:15:46.810 --> 00:15:50.230
of evidence that I noticed: first, the
lighting and color. Yes, both kylo and Rey

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:54.130
have the same fiery color tone on their
faces, but the lighting is different.

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:57.880
Rey looks like she's much closer to the
light source casting a harsher shadow on

00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:01.030
the right side of her face.
Meanwhile the light on Kylo's face is

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:04.840
more evenly spread, suggesting that the
light source is further away. Secondly,

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:08.380
look at the background. Rey's location
appears to be relatively stable, while

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:12.970
Kylo is surrounded by smoke and embers.
Wherever he is, it's currently on fire. I

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:16.270
actually think the shot of Rey is taken
from the campfire scene that we saw in

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:20.020
the behind the scenes footage, and her
saying I need someone to show me my

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:24.010
place in all this is her last ditch plea
to Luke to train her. And then finally,

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:28.990
listen to her audio again. "--to show me
my place, in all this." To me, that echo doesn't sound

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:32.590
natural, almost like it was added with an
audio filter in post-production to make

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:37.000
it sound like Rey was in an interior
location, further trying to pull off this

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.880
illusion that she and Kylo are facing
each other. I don't know, this just

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.910
reminds me a lot of the way that Rogue
One trailer ended, remember when they

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:47.710
made it look like Jyn Erso had gone to
the dark side. "What will you become?" You

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:51.340
can't always trust Star Wars trailers,
people. Like this could all be left on

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:54.190
the cutting room floor by December. Which
do you think is more likely in The Last

